  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "All five completed experiments use scgpt as the RNA encoder, so we have zero evidence about whether the learned RNA representation is actually critical or whether a simpler linear projection (PCA) would suffice. The best configuration so far is config_018 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc 0.5420). config_007 changes only the RNA encoder from scgpt to pca_n2000 while holding the image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (avgpool), fusion (weighted), and profile setting (multiprofile) constant. This gives a clean single-variable comparison that directly tests whether the RNA encoder is a meaningful design decision. If PCA performs comparably, the RNA representation is not a bottleneck and we can simplify the pipeline; if it performs substantially worse, it validates scgpt and focuses future search on other axes (aggregation, profile setting). Under a limited budget, resolving this fundamental representation question is more informative than, e.g., testing transformer aggregation, because the RNA encoder choice affects the entire model family."
}

